-- title:
--   Horizontal prime of the crossing model through V-varpiᵈ
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain (a domain which is a discrete valuation ring and is adically complete for its maximal ideal), let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $e, d$ be natural numbers with $1 \le e$, $1 \le d$ and $d + 1 \le e$. Write $R =$ `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)` for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ (indexed by `Fin 2`) by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \varpi^{e}$, let $U$ and $V$ denote the distinguished elements `U (ϖ ^ e)`, `V (ϖ ^ e)` of $R$, whose product is the image of the constant $\varpi^{e}$, and for $w \in W$ let `const (ϖ ^ e) w` be the image in $R$ of the constant power series $w$. The assertion is that there exists a prime ideal $Q$ of $R$ with the following properties: $Q \neq 0$; the image of $\varpi$ in $R$ does not lie in $Q$; both $V - \varpi^{d}$ and $U - \varpi^{e-d}$ (constants understood via `const`) lie in $Q$; $Q$ is the only prime of $R$ that avoids the image of $\varpi$ and contains $V - \varpi^{d}$; the quotient $R/Q$ is a free and finite $W$-module of rank $1$; the norm over $W$ of the class of $V$ in $R/Q$ equals $\varpi^{d}$; and the localisation of $R/(V - \varpi^{d})$ at $Q$ has length $1$ over the local ring $R_Q$.
--
--   This describes the $W$-point $(U,V) = (\varpi^{e-d}, \varpi^{d})$ of the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \varpi^{e})$, the standard local model at a point where two branches of a modular curve cross, and identifies it as the unique horizontal (i.e. not containing $\varpi$) prime through $V - \varpi^{d}$, together with the rank, norm and multiplicity data attached to it. It is used in the computation of leading residues and of norms of unit parts on the crossing model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_prime_V_sub_const_pow_mem.lean

